#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0338 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "dataset ADLBC. Columns STUDYID(Char), USUBJID(Char), PARAMCD(Char), MCRIT1(Char), MCRIT1ML(Char). ONE row: `CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | RESPONSE | HIGH`. Both halves of the pair are declared, so the second conjunct `not var_exists('MCRIT1ML')` is FALSE and the rule is silent. The two wildcard patterns are disjoint, so this still yields exactly one expansion (y=1), not two."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col MCRIT1 type=Char
col MCRIT1ML type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | RESPONSE | HIGH
